---
import { Code } from "astro:components";
import ProjectPage from "../../layouts/ProjectPage.astro";

const codeTheme = "github-dark-dimmed";

const docs = "https://super-yojan.dev/Zorvane/";
const repo = "https://github.com/Super-Yojan/Zorvane";
const zenoh = "https://github.com/Super-Yojan/Zorvane/blob/main/simulator/ZENOH.md";
---

<ProjectPage
    title="Zorvane"
    description="Zorvane is the world simulator split out of Terra. Terrain, physics, cameras, and a Zenoh bridge. The default world is the practice town."
    lede="The world those rovers drive in. Terrain, physics, cameras, and the Zenoh bridge."
    figureLabel="Fig. 09 — Practice town"
    figureAlt="The default Zorvane world, a practice town, with the terra-ground rover on a road."
    poster="/media/zorvane/town.png"
    posterWidth={960}
    posterHeight={540}
    figureNote="Default world"
    primary={{ href: "#quick-start", label: "Get Started" }}
    secondary={{ href: docs, label: "Read the Docs" }}
    aboutTitle="The world, split out of Terra."
    sectionId="quick-start"
    sectionTitle="Quick start."
    sectionLede="Rust 1.85 or newer, a C toolchain, and the Bevy window libraries. The figure is the practice town, not the rover CAD."
    links={[
        { href: docs, label: "Zorvane manual" },
        { href: repo, label: "Zorvane on GitHub" },
        { href: zenoh, label: "Zenoh topics" },
        { href: "/projects/argos", label: "ARGOS" },
    ]}
>
    <Fragment slot="prose">
        <p>
            Zorvane is the platform-agnostic world and competition simulator
            extracted from Terra. Terra is the vehicle body.
            <a href="/projects/argos">ARGOS</a> is the fleet operator. This
            repository is the world: terrain, physics, cameras, and the Zenoh
            bridge those operators already speak.
        </p>
        <p>
            The default world is the practice town in the figure. The default
            body is <code>terra-ground</code>.             The mesh for that body,
            <code>rover.glb</code>, is Git LFS, about 118 MB, and it lives in
            this repository. Shared crates stay in Terra and are git
            dependencies.
        </p>
        <p>
            One peer listens on <code>tcp/127.0.0.1:7447</code>. The prefix is
            <code>terra/rover</code>. There is no router. With Zenoh on, a
            client selects waypoint autonomy and sends a goal on the existing
            rover topics. The rover plans around obstacles in its
            depth-derived occupancy map. An unknown or unreachable route holds
            motion until a safe route exists. When a route exists, its points
            are published as <code>global_route</code> in
            <code>autonomy/status</code>.
        </p>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="facts">
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Default world</dt>
            <dd>Practice town</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Default body</dt>
            <dd><code>terra-ground</code></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Listen</dt>
            <dd><code>tcp/127.0.0.1:7447</code></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Prefix</dt>
            <dd><code>terra/rover</code></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Fleet</dt>
            <dd>0–32 rovers</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
            <dt class="t-label">Mesh</dt>
            <dd><code>rover.glb</code>, Git LFS, ~118 MB</dd>
        </div>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="steps">
        <li>
            <p class="t-label">01</p>
            <div class="prose">
                <h3>Install the toolchain</h3>
                <p>
                    Rust stable new enough for edition 2024 (1.85 or newer;
                    1.99 is known to work), a C toolchain, pkg-config, and the
                    Bevy window libraries:
                </p>
                <Code
                    code={`sudo apt-get install -y pkg-config build-essential \\
  libwayland-dev libxkbcommon-dev libvulkan-dev \\
  libxcursor-dev libxrandr-dev libxi-dev libx11-xcb-dev \\
  libasound2-dev libudev-dev`}
                    lang="bash"
                    theme={codeTheme}
                    wrap={false}
                />
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p class="t-label">02</p>
            <div class="prose">
                <h3>Run the practice town</h3>
                <p>
                    <code>rover.glb</code> is Git LFS, about 118 MB. Clone
                    with <code>git lfs install</code> and
                    <code>git lfs pull</code>, then:
                </p>
                <Code code="cargo run -p zorvane" lang="bash" theme={codeTheme} wrap={false} />
                <p>
                    That is the town in the figure. The body is
                    <code>terra-ground</code>. A windowed run needs a display.
                </p>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p class="t-label">03</p>
            <div class="prose">
                <h3>The other two worlds</h3>
                <p>
                    <code>TERRA_TILES=1</code> loads the real-elevation patch.
                    <code>TERRA_NEXT=1</code> loads the NEXT practice pitch
                    instead: a 32 m square, Zatara in spawn slot 0 on
                    <code>terra-ground</code>, six tennis balls, two deposit
                    buckets. NEXT does not score a match. It turns the
                    practice town and the tiles off.
                </p>
                <p>
                    <code>TERRA_ROVER_COUNT</code> sets the fleet size, from 0
                    through 32. <code>ZORVANE_VEHICLE</code> selects a
                    registered body and defaults to <code>terra-ground</code>.
                </p>
            </div>
        </li>
        <li>
            <p class="t-label">04</p>
            <div class="prose">
                <h3>Headless smoke</h3>
                <p>
                    No window, no Zenoh, exit after the world schedule starts:
                </p>
                <Code
                    code="TERRA_HEADLESS=1 TERRA_ZENOH=0 ZORVANE_SMOKE=1 cargo run -p zorvane"
                    lang="bash"
                    theme={codeTheme}
                    wrap={false}
                />
                <p>
                    <code>TERRA_HEADLESS=1</code> disables winit and steps the
                    app on a timer. Rendering still asks Vulkan for a device.
                    lavapipe (<code>mesa-vulkan-drivers</code>) is enough.
                    Topics, including <code>cmd_vel</code>, <code>goal</code>,
                    cameras, and fleet, are listed in the Zenoh note.
                </p>
            </div>
        </li>
    </Fragment>
</ProjectPage>
